  "question": {
    "text": "Let C be a curve given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msqrt><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>.&nbsp;If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> is a point on C, such that the tangent at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> has slope <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>, then a point through which the normal at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> passes, is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ZWCCv",
      "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi> </mi><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "Nk5Pg",
      "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi> </mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "dh71n",
      "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi> </mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "dcF3B",
      "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi> </mi><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msqrt><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> <math><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math><br /><br />So, <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math><br /><br />Equation of normal at&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br />i.e., <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> <math><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>17</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Hence only option&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;is satisfying the equation.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
